        {
            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "> Do you have any solution for that in mind that I could perhaps apply to my config? If not I'll leave it as is\r\n\r\nI am not sure what solution you'd expect here. 'mini.git' tracks and will continue to track only buffers corresponding to an actual files on disk. So expect to only have Git information in statusline for such buffers.\r\n\r\nTo avoid situations like immediately after `:edit my-new-file`:\r\n- Create file beforehand (like inside 'mini.files', with `:!touch my-new-file`, or other tools) and then it with `:edit my-new-file`.\r\n- Call `:edit` without arguments or reenter the buffer after `:edit my-new-file` - `:write`.",
